# Unity plugin DLLs before Editor work

`Assets/Plugins/Core/*.dll` are gitignored and must be regenerated locally.

**Before the first Unity action in a session** (Unity MCP, `Assets/Scripts/`,
scenes, prefabs, UXML/USS, play mode, or `unity-e2e-run`), read and follow
`.claude/skills/unity-plugins/SKILL.md`.

That means running `python scripts/unity/ensure_plugin_dlls.py` from the
project root and stopping if it fails. Do not commit plugin DLLs.
